\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion} 
 We have presented a remarkably tight $\dHI$-$\mHI$ relation with the largest sample examined to date. The sample covers around five orders of magnitude in \hi mass, ten $B$-band magnitudes, three orders of magnitude in $\mHI/{\rm L}_B$, and one order in $\dHI/{\rm D}_{25}$.  We have investigated whether the scatter about the $\dHI$-$\mHI$ relation depends on any of these parameters but found that it does not. We have found that the $\dHI$-$\mHI$ relation is a consequence of the self-similar $\SHI$ radial profiles of galaxies.  In this section we discuss the implications of these results on the mechanisms that drive the $\dHI$-$\mHI$ relation.

